Collagen is a fibrous protein found in many tissues in animals.
Fig. 2.1 shows the composition of a collagen fibre.
{{figure:figure_2_1.webp}}

parts.stem:
Table 2.1 shows the DNA triplets in the two strands of DNA in part of a gene that codes for one of the polypeptides in collagen.
{{figure:reviewed_table_1.png}}

Table 2.2 shows the triplets of bases in **DNA** and the amino acids for which they code.
The table can be used to determine the sequence of the amino acids in a polypeptide.
{{figure:table-2-2-original.webp}}
